    "lineage": "README names it 'SFERESv2' (Mouret and Doncieux, CEC 2010), implying a v1 predecessor not present in the tree; old docs at 'https://github.com/jbmouret/sferes2/wiki' (earlier repo location); README says 'Map-Elites (we will soon integrate a more flexible version in the master branch of sferes_v2): https://github.com/sferes2/map_elites'; optional modules nn2 (evolvable neural networks) and fastsim (khepera-like simulator). Bundles Nikolaus Hansen's C CMA-ES, Pete Goodliffe's dbg library, Melissa O'Neill's randutils, and Thomas Nagy's waf. || main loop (reader, from the code): Ea::run() creates a random population, then for _gen from 0 to Params::pop::nb_gen (unless stop()) calls the concrete algorithm's epoch() (e.g. RankSimple: keep the top keep_rate*size, refill the rest by rank-biased parent selection, cross(), mutate(), evaluate the new ones via _eval_pop, apply fitness modifiers, partial_sort by fitness), refreshes every stat in the boost::fusion stat vector, and every dump_period generations serializes the stats to res_dir/gen_<N>."
   },
